---
import AboutTable from './AboutTable.astro';
import { profileSkillGroups } from '../data/profile';
import { worksData } from '../data/works';
---

<article class="about-page">
  <h1 class="about-page__title">About</h1>

  <section class="about-page__section about-page__section--intro">
    <div class="about-page__body">
      <p>Hi, I'm LI Zhongpeng, nobody writing code in this world.</p>

      <p>
        I am passionate about coding, building clean and pure products and exploring anything
        that sparks my curiosity, from code, products to music, films, and beyond.
      </p>

      <p>
        I'm passionate about all aspects of computer science, from the fundamental concepts to
        real-world applications. These all fascinate me and that's why I write blogs all about
        them.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="about-page__section">
    <AboutTable>
      <Fragment slot="eyebrow">Skills</Fragment>

      <Fragment slot="colgroup">
        <colgroup>
          <col class="about-table-block__col-area" />
          <col />
        </colgroup>
      </Fragment>

      <Fragment slot="head">
        <th>Area</th>
        <th>Tools</th>
      </Fragment>

      {
        profileSkillGroups.map((group) => (
          <tr>
            <th>{group.label}</th>
            <td>{group.items.join(', ')}</td>
          </tr>
        ))
      }
    </AboutTable>
  </section>

  <section class="about-page__section">
    <div class="about-page__body">
      <p>
        I'm mainly focus on front-end development, and I love the elegance and simplicity of
        Python and JavaScript, while keeping a strong curiosity about algorithms and the inner
        workings of computers. But anyway, I'm somewhat opposed to dynamic typing and mastering a
        strongly typed language is essential, which is what I'm pursuing, Pydantic, TypeScript,
        etc.
      </p>

      <p>
        I feel lucky to be learning and exploring what I truly love. I hope I can keep making
        progress, stay persistent, meet more outstanding people, and grow into a better version of
        myself.
      </p>

      <p>
        I am but a tiny bug, crawling through the vast machinery of life. I work, I struggle, only
        for quiet hope. Perhaps life holds no inherent meaning, but meaning is something we create,
        not something we find. Even a bug can choose to become more than what it was born to be.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="about-page__section">
    <AboutTable mobileMinWidth="760px">
      <Fragment slot="eyebrow">Works</Fragment>

      <Fragment slot="colgroup">
        <colgroup>
          <col class="about-table-block__col-project" />
          <col class="about-table-block__col-description" />
          <col class="about-table-block__col-stack" />
          <col class="about-table-block__col-links" />
        </colgroup>
      </Fragment>

      <Fragment slot="head">
        <th>Project</th>
        <th>Description</th>
        <th>Stack</th>
        <th>Links</th>
      </Fragment>

      {
        worksData.projects.map((project) => (
          <tr>
            <th>{project.name}</th>
            <td>{project.description}</td>
            <td>{project.tags.join(', ')}</td>
            <td>
              <div class="about-table-block__links">
                {Object.entries(project.links).map(([label, href]) => (
                  <a href={href} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
                    {label}
                  </a>
                ))}
              </div>
            </td>
          </tr>
        ))
      }
    </AboutTable>
  </section>

  <section class="about-page__section">
    <div class="about-page__body">
      <p>
        Life is like a journey of self-cultivation, where the key lies in the understanding of it
        yourself. Thanks for learn more about me:
      </p>

      <ul class="about-page__list">
        <li><strong>Outdoor and nature lover</strong> who enjoys hiking, climbing.</li>
        <li>
          Life lover who is passionate about thinking, writing blogs and <a href="/photos/">photography</a>.
        </li>
        <li>Bookworm who is passionate about computer science, politics, etc.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</article>

<style>
  .about-page {
    padding-top: 1.75rem;
    margin-bottom: 3.5rem;
  }

  .about-page__title {
    margin: 0 0 2rem;
    color: var(--color-heading);
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 1.7rem + 1.2vw, 2.5rem);
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    line-height: 1.05;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .about-page__section {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
  }

  .about-page__section--intro {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .about-page__body {
    max-width: none;
    color: var(--color-text);
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.9;
  }

  .about-page__body p {
    margin: 0 0 1.35rem;
  }

  .about-page__body a {
    color: var(--color-heading);
    text-decoration: none;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(128, 128, 128, 0.25);
    transition: border-color 0.2s ease, color 0.2s ease;
  }

  .about-page__body a:hover {
    color: var(--color-nav-hover);
    border-color: currentColor;
  }

  .about-page__list {
    margin: 1.2rem 0 0;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
  }

  .about-page__list li {
    margin-bottom: 0.85rem;
  }

</style>
